# LeakSanitizer suppressions for MaBoSS.
#
# Scope: this file contains only what is needed to keep the gating sanitizer
# job -- unit and regression tests -- clean. It is a to-do list, not a
# permanent exemption; delete each entry as the leak behind it is fixed.
#
# Applied automatically by ctest for a -DMABOSS_SANITIZE=... build, or by hand:
#     LSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=engine/tests/sanitizers/lsan.supp
#

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Parser leaks on error
#
# The grammar actions build the expression trees with raw pointers. When a
# parse is aborted -- a syntax error, or an action that throws, such as an
# unknown node or attribute -- the expressions already on the parser stack are
# not freed. Only the unit tests, which check that bad input is rejected, hit
# this; successful parses do not leak.
#
# Freeing them needs owning values (std::unique_ptr in the bison variants):
# a bison %destructor on the raw pointers would double free the values that a
# throwing action has already handed to another object.
leak:ctbndl::parser::parse
leak:rc::parser::parse
